    "result_text": "All 256 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `'<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` to `'<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>'`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the sole place `customerCode` is generated:\n- Rewrote `nextCustomerCode` to take both `city` and `lastName`. It now builds `CITY3` (upper-cased first three letters of the city) and `LAST3` (upper-cased first three of the last name), and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already in that city (matched case/whitespace-insensitively via the existing `normaliseIdentity` helper), replacing the old global owner count.\n- Extracted a small `prefix3` helper for the shared \"upper-cased first three chars\" logic.\n- Updated the call site to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode`** rebuild automatically: `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipNumber` composes `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` directly from `getCustomerCode()`, so the membership number now carries the new format with no code change \u2014 I only refreshed its javadoc example.\n\n**Docs/examples** in `openapi.yml` (customerCode + membershipNumber descriptions and examples) updated to reflect the new format.\n\nVerification: the new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 **256 tests, 0 failures**.",
